    {
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Diagrams are Mermaid source, drawn natively per surface: the browser runs mermaid.js; the terminal lays the same graph out with its own engine — and picks its strategy from measured shape (wide chains go left-to-right, tight meshes become a tree):"
        }
      ],
      "id": "fd-023",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "caption": "One Mermaid source, two native renderers.",
      "id": "fd-024",
      "source": "flowchart TD\n  Doc[PortableDoc] --> View(Reader)\n  Doc --> Edit([Studio])\n  Doc --> Tui{{Terminal}}\n  View --> Same[(One document)]\n  Edit --> Same\n  Tui --> Same",
      "type": "diagram"
    },
    {
      "caption": "A sequence diagram rides the lifeline ladder in the terminal.",
      "id": "fd-025",
      "source": "sequenceDiagram\n  Author->>Studio: edit block\n  Studio->>API: patch content\n  API-->>Reader: publish\n  API-->>TUI: same document",
      "type": "diagram"
    },
    {
      "id": "fd-026",
      "type": "divider"
